                  <additions>
                  <list>
                    <item xml:id="e1">
                    <desc>
                    Simple quire numbers, at the top, near the gutter of the first folio of a quire
                    </desc>
                    </item>
                    <item xml:id="a1">
                    <locus target="#101v" facs="102"/>
                    <desc type="OwnershipNote">
                    The owner, <foreign xml:lang="gez">ወልደ፡ አረጋዊ፡</foreign>, Walda Aragawi, is mentioned. The scribe, <foreign xml:lang="gez">ዓስበ፡ ጊዮርጊስ፡</foreign>, Asba Giyorgis, is mentioned
                    </desc>
                    </item>
                    <item xml:id="a2">
                    <locus target="#103v" facs="104"> f. 103, column two, top</locus>
                    <desc>
                    has a place to mention the patriarch of Alexandria as well as the Abuna of Ethiopia, but the spaces are left blank, in the latter case, and in the former, there is only the word <foreign xml:lang="gez">እገሌ፡</foreign>, “so and so.”
                    </desc>
                    </item>
                  </list>
                </additions>
